., "benzopyrene in smoke causes DNA mutations in lung cells"). Those specific claims are falsifiable, and if enough of them were overturned, the general conclusion would change. So, is the core idea scientific? Yes, because it generates specific, testable predictions that have been rigorously examined and have survived (in modified form) repeated attempts at falsification. The fact that it can be refined by evidence—not just protected—is the hallmark of a scientific, rather than a dogmatic, claim.
