ce. But it is still strong enough to guide reasonable action. The claim that "all foods are the same" is not supported by the evidence—it is a leap that ignores the consistent, convergent patterns we observe. You are right to demand higher standards. But the burden of proof has shifted: it is now more reasonable to believe that diet matters (with moderate certainty) than to believe it does not. That is where the science stands.
